1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:03,002
<i>Sir, we're here for the boxing class.</i>

2
00:00:03,086 --> 00:00:04,337
<i>Precious?</i>

3
00:00:04,421 --> 00:00:05,630
<i>Brandon?</i>

4
00:00:05,714 --> 00:00:07,590
<i>It's really nice to meet you.</i>

5
00:00:07,674 --> 00:00:09,718
<i>Do you think he's fit to be</i>
<i>a father figure to me?</i>

6
00:00:09,801 --> 00:00:11,594
<i>Are you still looking for a father?</i>

7
00:00:11,678 --> 00:00:13,096
<i>Of course!</i>

8
00:00:14,848 --> 00:00:17,559
<i>Mr. and Mrs. Chan-Li were very responsive.</i>

9
00:00:17,642 --> 00:00:20,854
<i>We just need to give them</i>
<i>something worth their investment.</i>

10
00:00:20,937 --> 00:00:22,355
- [PHONE RINGING]
<i>- And we need to focus.</i>

11
00:00:22,439 --> 00:00:25,984
[CHARM] <i>Didn't you tell Yani</i>
<i>you can't go to his exhibit?</i>

12
00:00:26,067 --> 00:00:28,028
[TONI] <i>I said I'd be there later.</i>

13
00:00:28,111 --> 00:00:30,405
[MARIELA]<i> It's Saturday.</i>
<i>Where are you going?</i>

14
00:00:30,488 --> 00:00:32,240
[ABI] <i>My boss is asking me</i>
<i>to come to work.</i>

15
00:00:32,323 --> 00:00:35,827
<i>Like I told you, Ma, I'll be like Abi.</i>

16
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:37,245
<i>I'm almost there.</i>

17
00:00:37,328 --> 00:00:38,788
<i>Just wait.</i>

18
00:00:38,872 --> 00:00:41,291
[BILLY]<i> She said she owns</i>
<i>an internet cafe.</i>

19
00:00:41,374 --> 00:00:43,001
- [JORDAN] <i>She could be lying.</i>
<i>- How's it going?</i>

20
00:00:43,084 --> 00:00:45,837
<i>- Did you find it?</i>
<i>- Yes, but it's closed now.</i>

21
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:49,424
<i>It's closed only because</i>
<i>she has debts to the landlady.</i>

22
00:00:49,507 --> 00:00:51,384
<i>The landlady said Abi's going to pay.</i>

23
00:00:51,468 --> 00:00:53,052
<i>She won't take anything back.</i>

24
00:00:53,136 --> 00:00:55,805
<i>Hey! Hey, those computers are mine!</i>

25
00:00:55,889 --> 00:00:57,182
<i>Those are my computers!</i>

26
00:00:57,265 --> 00:00:59,768
[TONI] <i>We didn't just get her computers.</i>

27
00:00:59,851 --> 00:01:01,811
<i>- Ta-da!</i>
<i>- These, too!</i>

28
00:01:01,895 --> 00:01:03,354
[BILLY] <i>Auntie Pres, this is really mine.</i>

29
00:01:03,438 --> 00:01:06,024
<i>She even pretended</i>
<i>to be your fan just to rob you!</i>

30
00:01:06,107 --> 00:01:08,068
[BILLY] <i>Just let her try doing that again.</i>

31
00:01:08,151 --> 00:01:09,986
<i>I'm not going to back down.</i>

32
00:01:18,745 --> 00:01:19,746
[BOTTLE THUDS]

33
00:01:24,417 --> 00:01:26,795
I'll get back at Billy.

34
00:01:26,878 --> 00:01:28,254
That witch.

35
00:01:28,338 --> 00:01:30,089
Relax.

36
00:01:30,173 --> 00:01:31,841
We'll get even with her. Don't worry.

37
00:01:33,009 --> 00:01:35,762
Come on, 'Bi. Check this out.

38
00:01:37,597 --> 00:01:38,556
- [BOTTLE THUDS]
- 'Bi.

39
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:40,517
Hey, what are you doing?

40
00:01:44,062 --> 00:01:48,191
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

41
00:01:48,274 --> 00:01:50,110
What did you do, Caloy?

42
00:01:50,193 --> 00:01:51,653
What's that?

43
00:01:52,153 --> 00:01:54,114
'Bi, I love you this much.

44
00:01:56,366 --> 00:01:57,492
- [CALOY EXHALES]
- [SIGHS]

45
00:01:57,575 --> 00:01:59,452
'Bi, you're always by my side.

46
00:01:59,536 --> 00:02:01,287
Everyone else has left me.

47
00:02:01,371 --> 00:02:02,747
I'm all alone.

48
00:02:02,831 --> 00:02:05,333
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

49
00:02:05,416 --> 00:02:06,709
But from now on…

50
00:02:06,793 --> 00:02:07,877
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

51
00:02:08,419 --> 00:02:10,046
…it's going to be you and me forever, 'Bi.

52
00:02:12,590 --> 00:02:14,425
You are permanently etched onto my heart.

53
00:02:17,053 --> 00:02:18,096
I love you.

54
00:02:20,014 --> 00:02:21,391
- [SOFT BLOW LANDS]
- Ouch…

55
00:02:22,225 --> 00:02:23,184
[GROANS]

56
00:02:23,852 --> 00:02:25,019
This is a fresh one!

57
00:02:25,103 --> 00:02:26,187
[GROANS]

58
00:02:26,896 --> 00:02:27,856
[INHALES SHARPLY]

59
00:02:27,939 --> 00:02:29,107
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

60
00:02:29,190 --> 00:02:30,066
[SIGHS]

61
00:02:33,278 --> 00:02:36,072
Hey, you're smiling.
You can't shake the butterflies, huh?

62
00:02:36,156 --> 00:02:37,198
[CHUCKLES DRYLY]

63
00:02:38,324 --> 00:02:39,534
Let me see that smile.

64
00:02:39,617 --> 00:02:40,952
What do you want?

65
00:02:41,494 --> 00:02:44,080
Want me to get your shoes back? Huh?

66
00:02:44,164 --> 00:02:46,124
I'll take care of it.
I'll go there right now!

67
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:49,335
Get my computers too while you're at it.

68
00:02:49,419 --> 00:02:51,754
If only Ms. Tere hadn't
sold them to Billy.

69
00:02:51,838 --> 00:02:52,672
Damn it.

70
00:02:52,755 --> 00:02:53,882
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

71
00:02:53,965 --> 00:02:55,633
W-Wait a minute. Where did they take them?

72
00:02:55,717 --> 00:02:57,886
They said they'll donate them.

73
00:02:57,969 --> 00:02:59,304
[CALOY SUCKS TEETH]

74
00:02:59,387 --> 00:03:03,141
B-But where are they giving them away?
We need them!

75
00:03:04,726 --> 00:03:06,185
Not anymore. Forget it.

76
00:03:06,269 --> 00:03:07,478
She can have them.

77
00:03:07,562 --> 00:03:09,606
I don't need them anymore.

78
00:03:09,689 --> 00:03:11,107
[HUFFS]

79
00:03:11,190 --> 00:03:12,525
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

80
00:03:12,609 --> 00:03:14,777
I have other plans for Billy.

81
00:03:14,861 --> 00:03:18,072
[MUSIC INTENSIFYING]

82
00:03:18,156 --> 00:03:19,198
[SNICKERS]

83
00:03:20,867 --> 00:03:27,332
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

84
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:14,921
[ROBBIE] Go, wash them.

85
00:04:15,004 --> 00:04:16,172
[GLASSES CLINKING IN DISTANCE]

86
00:04:17,006 --> 00:04:19,008
I'LL HOLD YOUR HAND IN THE MADNESS

87
00:04:19,092 --> 00:04:20,593
- No more orders coming in?
- [HUMMING]

88
00:04:20,677 --> 00:04:22,887
- [TENDER MUSIC PLAYING]
- [WOMAN CRYING]

89
00:04:22,971 --> 00:04:24,973
- [FRIEND 1] Cheers, girls.
- [FRIEND 2] Let's dance!

90
00:04:25,056 --> 00:04:25,932
[BOTTLES CLINK]

91
00:04:26,015 --> 00:04:27,892
- [SINGS] <i>Just lean…</i>
- [FRIEND 3] Here's to her!

92
00:04:27,976 --> 00:04:29,394
- [FRIEND 4] Come on!
- [FRIEND 5] Well?

93
00:04:29,477 --> 00:04:30,979
[HEELS CLACK]

94
00:04:32,772 --> 00:04:34,524
[WOMAN CRYING]

95
00:04:34,607 --> 00:04:35,483
[FRIEND 1] Let's do it!

96
00:04:35,566 --> 00:04:38,778
- [FRIEND 2] Smile!
<i>- Just lean on me</i>

97
00:04:38,861 --> 00:04:39,737
[HUMMING]

98
00:04:39,821 --> 00:04:42,532
[TENDER MUSIC CONTINUES]

99
00:04:42,615 --> 00:04:49,414
<i>Let's just dance To the beat of our hearts</i>

100
00:04:49,914 --> 00:04:51,582
- [SQUEALS] A perfect match!
- You naughty kid!

101
00:04:51,666 --> 00:04:54,043
Why haven't you bathed yet?
You're already stinky.

102
00:04:54,127 --> 00:04:55,003
[SNIFFS] Go take a bath!

103
00:04:55,086 --> 00:04:57,046
Billy, check it out. Auntie's blushing.

104
00:04:57,130 --> 00:04:58,006
Look at her!

105
00:05:02,302 --> 00:05:03,845
- Right?
- Oh my!

106
00:05:04,512 --> 00:05:06,222
When was this?

107
00:05:06,306 --> 00:05:07,682
- The other day.
- [PRECIOUS] Oh, wow!

108
00:05:07,765 --> 00:05:09,475
- [OLIVER YELPS]
- Teasing me, huh?

109
00:05:09,559 --> 00:05:11,311
You scared me! [EXHALES]

110
00:05:11,394 --> 00:05:12,437
- Auntie Pres…
- Yeah?

111
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:13,771
- You're all smiles here.
- So giddy!

112
00:05:13,855 --> 00:05:14,689
Oh, please!

113
00:05:14,772 --> 00:05:17,150
- Your smile's so beautiful!
- He should court you now.

114
00:05:17,233 --> 00:05:18,067
It'll be fun.

115
00:05:18,151 --> 00:05:19,360
Wow! [CHUCKLES]

116
00:05:19,444 --> 00:05:22,822
I've never seen you smile
like this before.

117
00:05:22,905 --> 00:05:24,324
- Can I see it?
- Show us, show us.

118
00:05:24,866 --> 00:05:26,659
- It's not like that.
- It is!

119
00:05:26,743 --> 00:05:28,077
- It isn't.
- Do it properly.

120
00:05:28,161 --> 00:05:28,995
That was it.

121
00:05:29,078 --> 00:05:31,205
- Show us, show us!
- Who's this?

122
00:05:31,289 --> 00:05:33,374
- That man you're with.
- [OLIVER] That's Sir Eric.

123
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:36,294
He was in the same restaurant
where we had lunch.

124
00:05:36,377 --> 00:05:38,629
- Mm!
- I joined him instead…

125
00:05:39,213 --> 00:05:41,883
so I wouldn't disturb Auntie!

126
00:05:41,966 --> 00:05:43,718
- Shush! You're so naughty!
- Ow, ow!

127
00:05:43,801 --> 00:05:46,763
- You might've disturbed him.
- Not really.

128
00:05:46,846 --> 00:05:50,767
- How was he, Auntie Pres?
- Okay. Sir Eric's kind.

129
00:05:50,850 --> 00:05:52,894
- No, I meant Brandon.
- Huh?

130
00:05:52,977 --> 00:05:54,062
Your date.

131
00:05:54,687 --> 00:05:56,147
- Was there a spark?
- There was!

132
00:05:56,230 --> 00:05:58,024
- Huge! Like electricity!
- Oh, really?

133
00:05:58,107 --> 00:05:59,692
- There was a spark!
- Is that so?

134
00:05:59,776 --> 00:06:01,277
- You saw it?
- There was no spark!

135
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:04,113
- [BILLY] There's none?
- [OLIVER] Pillow fight!

136
00:06:04,197 --> 00:06:06,574
- [BILLY SHRIEKING HAPPILY]
- [PRECIOUS] Come here!

137
00:06:06,657 --> 00:06:08,076
[OLIVER] Pillow fight! Pillow fight!

138
00:06:08,159 --> 00:06:11,037
- [PRECIOUS] Oliver, that hurts!
- Ahh!

139
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:13,873
Ah! No, sorry, sorry. No. Auntie Pres!

140
00:06:13,956 --> 00:06:15,666
- Ahh! Ahh!
- [BILLY] Auntie Pres!

141
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:17,585
- There was a spark!
- You're giddy!

142
00:06:17,668 --> 00:06:19,587
[PRECIOUS] Wait, wait! Let's take a break!

143
00:06:19,670 --> 00:06:21,089
Wait, wait, wait!

144
00:06:22,215 --> 00:06:23,841
[OLIVER CHUCKLES]

145
00:06:23,925 --> 00:06:25,802
- I'm tired.
- There's a spark!

146
00:06:25,885 --> 00:06:27,595
- That was a different smile.
- There's a spark?

147
00:06:27,678 --> 00:06:29,263
- No!
- Mm-hmm.

148
00:06:29,347 --> 00:06:30,973
- It was a giddy smile.
- It was different.

149
00:06:34,435 --> 00:06:39,899
[PAPERS RUSTLING]

150
00:06:42,151 --> 00:06:47,824
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

151
00:06:47,907 --> 00:06:50,993
Oliver? Hm, here's your lunch, okay?

152
00:06:51,077 --> 00:06:53,663
Finish it. Sometimes,
you don't eat your fruit.

153
00:06:53,746 --> 00:06:55,498
- Okay, Billy.
- All right.

154
00:06:57,125 --> 00:06:58,543
You ready?

155
00:06:58,626 --> 00:06:59,669
- Ready!
- [BILLY CLAPS]

156
00:06:59,752 --> 00:07:01,671
Ready. Okay.

157
00:07:01,754 --> 00:07:05,508
In your science module about life cycle,

158
00:07:05,591 --> 00:07:09,095
what does the stage
called "fledging" mean?

159
00:07:09,178 --> 00:07:12,056
"Fledging." Fledging is the stage

160
00:07:12,140 --> 00:07:16,269
where young birds leave their nest
to learn how to fly.

161
00:07:16,352 --> 00:07:18,104
Oh! Very good!

162
00:07:18,187 --> 00:07:22,024
Congratulations!
You win one million pesos!

163
00:07:22,108 --> 00:07:23,526
Very good!

164
00:07:23,609 --> 00:07:26,404
Just one million?
It should be five million!

165
00:07:26,487 --> 00:07:29,949
- I studied hard, you know.
- It can't be five million!

166
00:07:30,032 --> 00:07:33,411
It should actually be 10 million
because I memorized that.

167
00:07:33,494 --> 00:07:37,582
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

168
00:07:39,041 --> 00:07:42,545
I'm sorry I wasn't there
for your first boxing class.

169
00:07:42,628 --> 00:07:45,006
I'll make it up to you
next week, I promise.

170
00:07:45,631 --> 00:07:48,759
Billy, I understand you're busy.

171
00:07:48,843 --> 00:07:50,720
And I should get used to that.

172
00:07:51,762 --> 00:07:52,597
What?

173
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:55,975
What if I get accepted
into the University of Kingsley?

174
00:07:56,058 --> 00:07:58,352
Just you wait, Billy.

175
00:07:58,436 --> 00:08:01,481
When I become a successful
software engineer,

176
00:08:02,023 --> 00:08:04,400
I will take care of you.

177
00:08:05,318 --> 00:08:06,569
Is that so?

178
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:10,364
Okay! You have to take care of me, okay?

179
00:08:10,448 --> 00:08:11,491
But

180
00:08:11,574 --> 00:08:14,994
right now, I just want you to have fun,

181
00:08:15,077 --> 00:08:17,079
to achieve all your dreams,

182
00:08:17,163 --> 00:08:18,831
and to do whatever you want.

183
00:08:18,915 --> 00:08:20,208
I will take care of you.

184
00:08:20,791 --> 00:08:22,001
My dream?

185
00:08:22,084 --> 00:08:26,214
I also dream of going to America
to visit Papa's grave.

186
00:08:26,297 --> 00:08:29,342
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

187
00:08:30,676 --> 00:08:31,636
Okay.

188
00:08:33,262 --> 00:08:36,140
- Next? Okay.
- Yes. Next question.

189
00:08:39,644 --> 00:08:42,939
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

190
00:08:43,022 --> 00:08:46,150
- [SIGHING]
- [PHONE THUDS]

191
00:08:46,234 --> 00:08:47,735
[GATE CREAKS OPEN]

192
00:08:49,654 --> 00:08:50,738
Eric.

193
00:08:51,239 --> 00:08:53,157
What's this? [HUFFS]

194
00:08:53,783 --> 00:08:57,453
I trusted you.
I let you rent this apartment.

195
00:08:58,120 --> 00:09:00,998
But, apparently, you faked
your police clearance?

196
00:09:01,082 --> 00:09:02,166
This is the original!

197
00:09:02,250 --> 00:09:03,793
You have a hit!

198
00:09:04,835 --> 00:09:07,505
I called NLEA. They said
you were imprisoned in Canada.

199
00:09:07,588 --> 00:09:08,881
I'm sorry, ma'am.

200
00:09:09,757 --> 00:09:11,676
I really need a job.

201
00:09:11,759 --> 00:09:13,886
You'll have to look elsewhere.
You're fired!

202
00:09:13,970 --> 00:09:15,054
Get out!

203
00:09:15,137 --> 00:09:17,390
I can't lose my spot in the canteen!

204
00:09:17,473 --> 00:09:20,851
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

205
00:09:20,935 --> 00:09:21,936
Ma'am…

206
00:09:22,937 --> 00:09:24,897
I need to make it up to my kids.

207
00:09:30,319 --> 00:09:32,029
But this is Oliver.

208
00:09:37,368 --> 00:09:40,288
Ms. Billy, here is the list
of our employees

209
00:09:40,371 --> 00:09:42,582
whose contracts are expiring next month.

210
00:09:43,207 --> 00:09:44,625
Blaire's one of them.

211
00:09:44,709 --> 00:09:47,128
If we're looking for ways to save,

212
00:09:47,211 --> 00:09:50,047
to cut some losses, we can downsize.

213
00:09:50,131 --> 00:09:54,093
And since these employees'
contracts are ending,

214
00:09:54,176 --> 00:09:56,345
we technically have no commitment to them.

215
00:09:56,429 --> 00:09:59,432
Agatha, I have a commitment to them.

216
00:10:00,016 --> 00:10:02,476
They're the people behind our success.

217
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:05,771
And now that the company
is facing challenges,

218
00:10:06,897 --> 00:10:10,735
is it right for them to be casualties
just to cut our losses?

219
00:10:12,987 --> 00:10:14,071
No.

220
00:10:14,155 --> 00:10:16,782
It's just a bit impractical, Ms. Billy.

221
00:10:16,866 --> 00:10:19,410
We will renew all of their contracts.

222
00:10:20,077 --> 00:10:21,537
Okay, Ms. Billy.

223
00:10:21,621 --> 00:10:23,122
- Thank you.
- Thank you, Agatha.

224
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:30,379
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

225
00:10:32,131 --> 00:10:33,215
You need this.

226
00:10:36,594 --> 00:10:38,054
I missed this.

227
00:10:38,137 --> 00:10:39,472
Thank you.

228
00:10:39,555 --> 00:10:41,515
You make it look so easy.

229
00:10:41,599 --> 00:10:43,309
Being strong.

230
00:10:43,392 --> 00:10:44,727
Confident.

231
00:10:44,810 --> 00:10:45,936
Composed.

232
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:47,813
You're such a sweet-talker.

233
00:10:47,897 --> 00:10:49,065
You need something, don't you?

234
00:10:49,148 --> 00:10:50,608
- I don't.
- Hmm…

235
00:10:50,691 --> 00:10:52,151
I'm just telling the truth.

236
00:10:52,735 --> 00:10:53,778
I could say the same to you.

237
00:10:55,738 --> 00:10:57,114
We got this.

238
00:10:57,198 --> 00:10:58,157
We do.

239
00:11:00,618 --> 00:11:02,745
By the way, how's Grandpa Jude?

240
00:11:04,205 --> 00:11:05,039
He's okay.

241
00:11:06,540 --> 00:11:07,458
Here.

242
00:11:09,001 --> 00:11:10,002
Oh no!

243
00:11:11,003 --> 00:11:12,171
Is he all right?

244
00:11:12,254 --> 00:11:13,714
They didn't find anything in the X-ray.

245
00:11:13,798 --> 00:11:15,758
- Sure?
- He's okay.

246
00:11:16,842 --> 00:11:18,260
Okay, good.

247
00:11:19,011 --> 00:11:21,597
They're becoming negligent.

248
00:11:22,181 --> 00:11:24,809
That's why I'm looking
for a better facility.

249
00:11:25,393 --> 00:11:26,852
So meaning,

250
00:11:27,645 --> 00:11:28,646
somewhere more expensive.

251
00:11:33,692 --> 00:11:36,612
Mm. Come on, we'll share.

252
00:11:36,695 --> 00:11:38,489
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

253
00:11:38,572 --> 00:11:40,241
[BILLY GRUNTS SOFTLY]

254
00:11:40,324 --> 00:11:41,367
[JORDAN] Cheers.

255
00:11:44,328 --> 00:11:46,122
- Mm.
- See?

256
00:11:46,831 --> 00:11:48,040
Chief?

257
00:11:48,124 --> 00:11:49,542
We're ready.

258
00:11:50,126 --> 00:11:50,960
Okay.

259
00:11:51,043 --> 00:11:52,962
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

260
00:11:53,045 --> 00:11:54,588
- Congratulations.
- Thank you so much.

261
00:11:54,672 --> 00:11:56,298
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

262
00:11:56,382 --> 00:11:58,926
I know we made the right decision
choosing you.

263
00:11:59,009 --> 00:12:01,387
We are so excited for this collaboration.

264
00:12:01,470 --> 00:12:04,849
Well, I'm just so, so grateful
I did not take the bait!

265
00:12:04,932 --> 00:12:07,184
Yes, because the original idea

266
00:12:07,268 --> 00:12:11,021
came from the newest member
of the Pebblng family,

267
00:12:11,105 --> 00:12:12,731
and not from that Billy.

268
00:12:12,815 --> 00:12:16,318
Well, she's a gem, for sure,
so don't let her get away.

269
00:12:16,402 --> 00:12:18,821
Oh, ma'am, thank you so much.

270
00:12:18,904 --> 00:12:22,324
And with that, cheers! Cheers!

271
00:12:22,408 --> 00:12:24,952
- Cheers! Cheers!
- Cheers! Cheers!

272
00:12:25,035 --> 00:12:28,456
Sir, cheers!
Morrie! Congratulations to us!

273
00:12:28,539 --> 00:12:29,457
[WINE GLASSES CLINK]

274
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:31,876
I love to travel, so…

275
00:12:31,959 --> 00:12:34,837
What if a destination wedding?

276
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:37,631
Like, a wedding in Siargao
if the couple are surfers.

277
00:12:37,715 --> 00:12:39,300
That's a good idea,

278
00:12:39,383 --> 00:12:41,677
but we have to think of the budget.

279
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:43,387
Of course, it'll be a destination wedding,

280
00:12:43,471 --> 00:12:45,806
so we can't fly all the guests, unless…

281
00:12:45,890 --> 00:12:47,266
we have sponsors.

282
00:12:47,349 --> 00:12:48,767
Or…

283
00:12:48,851 --> 00:12:50,853
we can make it into a fashion event!

284
00:12:52,980 --> 00:12:56,233
What if we brand our wedding events?

285
00:12:56,859 --> 00:12:58,986
I mean, the famous event.

286
00:12:59,528 --> 00:13:04,825
Let's have famous designers,
event stylists,

287
00:13:04,909 --> 00:13:06,160
and caterers on board.

288
00:13:06,744 --> 00:13:10,289
Okay. That's something we can explore.

289
00:13:10,372 --> 00:13:11,373
Toni?

290
00:13:11,457 --> 00:13:16,545
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

291
00:13:16,629 --> 00:13:18,881
Ah! I love cruises.

292
00:13:20,508 --> 00:13:24,720
But Yani was born
in the Year of the Tiger,

293
00:13:24,803 --> 00:13:30,476
so he has a high risk
of injuries and accidents this year.

294
00:13:30,559 --> 00:13:34,772
He's asked to be careful when traveling
or when doing anything near water.

295
00:13:36,941 --> 00:13:38,984
- What?
- Huh?

296
00:13:39,068 --> 00:13:40,736
A wedding on a cruise ship.

297
00:13:41,737 --> 00:13:42,947
Ahh…

298
00:13:43,030 --> 00:13:45,449
- Ah…
- Oh, okay.

299
00:13:45,533 --> 00:13:47,409
How's your eye?

300
00:13:48,035 --> 00:13:50,871
I'm okay, chief!
Look, it's basically gone now.

301
00:13:51,664 --> 00:13:52,706
Girls,

302
00:13:53,666 --> 00:13:56,001
thank you
for going the extra mile for this.

303
00:13:56,085 --> 00:13:59,838
I'm sorry we got to a point
where someone got hurt.

304
00:14:02,383 --> 00:14:05,219
[TONI] We all believe in LoveList.

305
00:14:05,302 --> 00:14:06,512
I'm okay.

306
00:14:08,639 --> 00:14:11,225
That Abi's just so irritating.

307
00:14:11,308 --> 00:14:13,185
If she hadn't stolen LoveFeast,

308
00:14:13,269 --> 00:14:16,522
then we would've been launching it today.

309
00:14:17,523 --> 00:14:19,191
There is nothing we can do.

310
00:14:19,942 --> 00:14:24,572
What won't change is we're getting closer
to our meeting with the investors,

311
00:14:24,655 --> 00:14:27,992
so we have no choice but to
come up with a solid plan today.

312
00:14:28,075 --> 00:14:31,829
Um, I think it's too late for that.

313
00:14:32,496 --> 00:14:34,123
- [TONI] Why?
- [VALERIE] Look.

314
00:14:34,790 --> 00:14:41,589
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

315
00:14:42,423 --> 00:14:43,966
[GROANS SOFTLY]

316
00:14:44,049 --> 00:14:45,759
Our would-be investors.

317
00:14:47,219 --> 00:14:48,470
Huh…

318
00:14:48,554 --> 00:14:51,181
That list! That was on my laptop!

319
00:14:51,932 --> 00:14:56,103
Chief, you had me make a company profile
for each investor, remember?

320
00:14:58,939 --> 00:15:00,774
Okay, that's enough!

321
00:15:00,858 --> 00:15:02,693
- We have pizza!
- Have a break first.

322
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:04,695
Pizza break!

323
00:15:04,778 --> 00:15:08,282
- [RALPH] Take a break first.
- [JORDAN] Pizza?

324
00:15:09,199 --> 00:15:10,284
[MOUTHS] Thank you.

325
00:15:13,454 --> 00:15:14,872
Dude.

326
00:15:14,955 --> 00:15:16,373
Got any ideas?

327
00:15:17,583 --> 00:15:18,876
Hmm!

328
00:15:18,959 --> 00:15:22,338
What if you do the opposite of LoveFeast?

329
00:15:22,421 --> 00:15:23,464
FeastLove?

330
00:15:23,964 --> 00:15:24,798
No.

331
00:15:24,882 --> 00:15:28,010
Instead of helping couples, you know,

332
00:15:28,093 --> 00:15:30,638
to get married, to get together,
and stuff, but…

333
00:15:30,721 --> 00:15:33,015
Help couples break up, I guess?

334
00:15:33,098 --> 00:15:35,225
The-- The toxic ones.

335
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:37,269
- Hm, babe.
- Hm.

336
00:15:38,103 --> 00:15:41,357
Babe, we're LoveList.

337
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:43,067
Your suggestion's bad.

338
00:15:43,150 --> 00:15:45,653
- The boss won't approve that.
- Come on, Ralph.

339
00:15:45,736 --> 00:15:49,239
I'm sure you know how stressful it can be
to save a business.

340
00:15:49,323 --> 00:15:51,825
Don't you have any more ideas?

341
00:15:51,909 --> 00:15:54,244
Or you don't know anything
'cause you're a rich kid.

342
00:15:55,245 --> 00:15:59,208
Hey! It's good that my boyfriend
is very supportive,

343
00:15:59,291 --> 00:16:00,793
even though he isn't part of our business.

344
00:16:00,876 --> 00:16:02,252
Mmm!

345
00:16:02,336 --> 00:16:03,796
I'm jelly.

346
00:16:05,589 --> 00:16:06,924
Chief.

347
00:16:07,007 --> 00:16:10,344
Even if we come up with a concept,

348
00:16:10,427 --> 00:16:13,347
who are we gonna present the pitch to?

349
00:16:13,430 --> 00:16:16,183
They already stole our potential
investors too.

350
00:16:16,266 --> 00:16:17,768
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

351
00:16:19,687 --> 00:16:21,313
[RALPH] Hm? All right!

352
00:16:22,189 --> 00:16:23,273
The gang's all here.

353
00:16:23,941 --> 00:16:25,442
Can we talk?

354
00:16:25,526 --> 00:16:31,407
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

355
00:16:31,490 --> 00:16:32,908
Hello, Ms. Lucy!

356
00:16:32,992 --> 00:16:34,410
Oh, Oliver!

357
00:16:34,493 --> 00:16:35,536
Is Sir Eric here?

358
00:16:42,209 --> 00:16:43,919
- Hey, Oliver.
- Hello, Sir Eric!

359
00:16:44,003 --> 00:16:45,254
I have already written an essay

360
00:16:45,337 --> 00:16:48,424
for my application
to the University of Kingsley.

361
00:16:48,507 --> 00:16:50,718
Is it all right if you give it a read?

362
00:16:50,801 --> 00:16:52,803
I don't want to bother my sister with it.

363
00:16:52,886 --> 00:16:55,764
As for Auntie, she said it's good.

364
00:16:55,848 --> 00:16:58,434
Sir, maybe you could give me
some suggestions?

365
00:16:58,517 --> 00:17:00,102
All right. I'll go over it later.

366
00:17:00,185 --> 00:17:01,270
Thank you!

367
00:17:01,353 --> 00:17:06,567
- [SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]
- [FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

368
00:17:07,401 --> 00:17:08,277
Eric.

369
00:17:09,403 --> 00:17:10,571
[SIGHS]

370
00:17:11,321 --> 00:17:14,033
I hope I don't lose my business
because of this.

371
00:17:14,116 --> 00:17:15,701
I'll be careful, ma'am.

372
00:17:15,784 --> 00:17:18,912
Why don't you just tell
your child the truth?

373
00:17:19,621 --> 00:17:20,748
I tried to.

374
00:17:20,831 --> 00:17:22,875
But my eldest doesn't want
to listen to me.

375
00:17:23,459 --> 00:17:26,003
I also think that if I want
to make it up to them,

376
00:17:26,086 --> 00:17:27,796
and for them to forgive me,

377
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:30,632
I shouldn't use it,
not in that way.

378
00:17:31,884 --> 00:17:33,260
For now… [EXHALES DEEPLY]

379
00:17:35,137 --> 00:17:36,555
…my youngest and I

380
00:17:37,181 --> 00:17:38,599
are doing just fine.

381
00:17:39,558 --> 00:17:41,518
My eldest and I will be
on good terms soon.

382
00:17:41,602 --> 00:17:42,978
How?

383
00:17:43,062 --> 00:17:46,940
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

384
00:17:47,024 --> 00:17:48,984
But this isn't right!

385
00:17:49,068 --> 00:17:51,236
It's better if you just quit
already, Toni!

386
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:52,863
Let's just stop this!

387
00:17:52,946 --> 00:17:54,114
[TONI SCOFFS]

388
00:17:54,198 --> 00:17:55,699
You want me to resign

389
00:17:55,783 --> 00:17:57,868
just when our marriage
is right around the corner?

390
00:17:57,951 --> 00:17:58,827
Are you serious?

391
00:17:58,911 --> 00:18:00,621
And it's because you don't
spend time with me.

392
00:18:00,704 --> 00:18:02,706
Who's more important? Me or your job?

393
00:18:04,374 --> 00:18:05,375
Toni?

394
00:18:06,210 --> 00:18:07,044
Yani?

395
00:18:07,127 --> 00:18:08,045
Is everything okay?

396
00:18:08,128 --> 00:18:10,464
Good thing you're here, Billy.
Join our conversation.

397
00:18:10,547 --> 00:18:12,841
You're a part of our relationship anyway.

398
00:18:12,925 --> 00:18:16,053
Isn't that right?
You're prioritizing this job over me.

399
00:18:16,804 --> 00:18:18,472
Yani, it's not like that.

400
00:18:19,723 --> 00:18:20,724
She's doing this for you.

401
00:18:20,808 --> 00:18:22,309
She's doing this for the
future of the two--

402
00:18:22,392 --> 00:18:24,353
No, she's doing this for you.

403
00:18:24,436 --> 00:18:26,146
That's why she got hurt.

404
00:18:26,230 --> 00:18:28,565
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

405
00:18:28,649 --> 00:18:31,485
Yani, I'm sorry she got hurt.

406
00:18:31,568 --> 00:18:33,237
She was just trying to help so that--

407
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:34,613
So that you could settle your score.

408
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:37,074
It was for the company.

409
00:18:37,699 --> 00:18:39,993
That the three of us worked so hard for.

410
00:18:40,077 --> 00:18:42,788
That is now also helping
a lot of employees.

411
00:18:43,413 --> 00:18:46,625
- Billy, she doesn't need LoveList.
- Hold up.

412
00:18:47,876 --> 00:18:50,129
If not for LoveList,
the two of you wouldn't have met.

413
00:18:50,212 --> 00:18:51,755
I can provide for her!

414
00:18:51,839 --> 00:18:53,841
I just need her to trust me a little.

415
00:18:53,924 --> 00:18:56,718
Yani, this isn't about
the ability to provide.

416
00:18:56,802 --> 00:18:58,178
It's about purpose.

417
00:18:58,262 --> 00:19:01,348
And Toni found that purpose
here at LoveList.

418
00:19:01,932 --> 00:19:03,600
Now we're talking about purpose?

419
00:19:03,684 --> 00:19:04,643
All right, then!

420
00:19:04,726 --> 00:19:05,602
[INHALES DEEPLY]

421
00:19:06,728 --> 00:19:08,021
Toni, make a choice.

422
00:19:09,022 --> 00:19:10,649
Your purpose or me?

423
00:19:11,316 --> 00:19:12,901
Love, don't do this to me--

424
00:19:12,985 --> 00:19:14,403
No, no. Make a choice.

425
00:19:15,863 --> 00:19:17,656
Toni, your purpose or me?

426
00:19:17,739 --> 00:19:23,829
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

427
00:19:32,671 --> 00:19:39,178
[SOMBER ROCK MUSIC PLAYING]

428
00:19:41,638 --> 00:19:42,556
Toni…

429
00:19:54,568 --> 00:20:01,074
["MAG-ISA LANG AKO"
BY SHANIAH ROLLO PLAYING]

430
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:23,847
["MAG-ISA LANG AKO" CONTINUES]

431
00:20:38,779 --> 00:20:45,744
["MAG-ISA LANG AKO" CONTINUES]

432
00:21:00,717 --> 00:21:06,265
["MAG-ISA LANG AKO" CONTINUES]

433
00:21:22,614 --> 00:21:28,704
["MAG-ISA LANG AKO" CONTINUES]

434
00:21:33,625 --> 00:21:36,920
<i>There are many kinds of love.</i>

435
00:21:37,004 --> 00:21:41,675
<i>♪ Baby, I won't be long ♪</i>

436
00:21:41,758 --> 00:21:42,718
<i>Heart-pounding.</i>

437
00:21:42,801 --> 00:21:44,928
<i>This love song is really good.</i>

438
00:21:45,012 --> 00:21:48,307
<i>It's not finished yet. And it's not a</i>
<i>love song. It's a friendship song.</i>

439
00:21:49,099 --> 00:21:50,183
<i>Hmm…</i>

440
00:21:50,267 --> 00:21:51,977
<i>There's also longing.</i>

441
00:21:52,060 --> 00:21:53,937
<i>Thanks again for volunteering.</i>

442
00:21:54,438 --> 00:21:56,440
<i>Anytime. It's for them.</i>

443
00:21:56,940 --> 00:21:58,692
<i>And love full sacrifices.</i>

444
00:21:58,775 --> 00:21:59,735
<i>I'm Melissa.</i>

445
00:21:59,818 --> 00:22:02,863
<i>I'm having second thoughts</i>
<i>about my wedding.</i>

446
00:22:02,946 --> 00:22:04,364
<i>My dad doesn't approve of him.</i>

447
00:22:04,448 --> 00:22:08,452
<i>We celebrate the unique love story</i>
<i>behind each one.</i>

448
00:22:08,535 --> 00:22:10,329
<i>How do we fund that?</i>

449
00:22:10,412 --> 00:22:12,831
[CAMILLE] <i>We have to think</i>
<i>about the entire event.</i>

450
00:22:12,914 --> 00:22:15,042
<i>Abi, ideas, please.</i>

451
00:22:15,125 --> 00:22:17,210
<i>Uh, ideas…</i>

452
00:22:17,294 --> 00:22:19,671
<i>- What are you doing here?!</i>
<i>- So what's the update on your computers?</i>

453
00:22:19,755 --> 00:22:22,841
<i>You just won't let it go.</i>
<i>Why do you even care about the computers?</i>

454
00:22:22,924 --> 00:22:24,051
<i>One of the computers</i>

455
00:22:24,134 --> 00:22:26,219
<i>has our pictures and videos on it.</i>

456
00:22:26,303 --> 00:22:27,721
<i>Find that computer, okay?</i>

457
00:22:27,804 --> 00:22:29,765
<i>Every single picture and video</i>
<i>on it has to be deleted!</i>

458
00:22:29,848 --> 00:22:34,227
<i>You know no one can ever find out</i>
<i>that we're connected!</i>
